// Worked example 1: the Recipe box project, described in recipe-box.md.
// A draft for human review: every line comes from a file named in recipe-box.md.

model recipe-box: Recipe box
  > A small web app where home cooks save recipes, plan the week's meals and get the shopping
    list by email.

audiences exec "Executive", manager "Manager" (default), engineer "Engineer" (code)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- elements

cook: Home cook | Plans meals in a browser [person]
  > Saves recipes, plans the week and asks for a shopping list.

recipe-box: Recipe box | Recipes, meal plans and shopping lists [system]
  > Three parts that start together: the web app, the recipe API and the database.
  @exec: | Our meal planning product
  @engineer >> `compose.yaml` starts `web`, `api` and `db`. Only `web` is published, on port
    3000.

  web: Web app | The screens cooks use [service]
    icon web
    > Shows recipes and the weekly plan, and sends every change to the recipe API.
    @engineer: | recipe-web, React 19 and Vite
    @engineer >> Built by `web/Dockerfile` and served by nginx on port 3000, which passes
      `/api/*` on to `api:8000`.

  api: Recipe API | Keeps recipes and plans, builds shopping lists [service]
    icon api
    > Saves recipes and meal plans, and turns a week's plan into a shopping list.
    @exec: Recipe service | Where the planning happens
    @engineer: | recipe-api, FastAPI :8000
    @engineer >> Routes in `api/routes/`: `recipes.py`, `plans.py` and `lists.py`.

    recipes: Recipe handling | Saves and searches recipes [module]
      @engineer: | api/routes/recipes.py
      @engineer >> `GET` and `POST /api/recipes`, `GET /api/recipes/search?q=`.

    planner: Meal planner | Turns a week's plan into a list [module]
      @engineer: | api/routes/plans.py, api/routes/lists.py
      @engineer >> `PUT /api/plans/{week}` and `POST /api/lists/send`.

    mailer: Mailer | Sends the shopping list [module]
      @engineer: | api/mail.py
      @engineer >> Reads `MAIL_API_KEY` and `MAIL_FROM` from the environment.

  db: Recipe database | Every recipe and meal plan [store]
    > Recipes, their ingredients, and each week's plan.
    @engineer: | PostgreSQL 16
    @engineer >> The `db` service in `compose.yaml`, with the volume `pgdata`. Tables come from
      `api/migrations/`.

// Unsure: the project names no email provider; `MAIL_API_KEY` suggests a hosted one.
mail: Email service | Delivers email [external]
  > An outside email provider.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- relationships

cook plans meals in web
web sends recipes to recipes
  @engineer: calls /api/recipes on
web sends weekly plans to planner
  @engineer: calls /api/plans on
web asks for the shopping list from planner
  @engineer: POSTs /api/lists/send to
recipes saves recipes in db
planner reads recipes from db
planner saves meal plans in db
planner hands the shopping list to mailer
mailer sends the shopping list through mail
  @engineer: POSTs the message to
mail emails the shopping list to cook

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- views

view big-picture: Big picture
  show cook, recipe-box +1, mail
  > Who uses Recipe box, its three parts, and the one outside service it needs.

view inside-api: Inside the recipe API
  show cook, web, api +1, db, mail
  @exec: How planning works

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- scenarios

scenario send-list: Sending the shopping list
  > From pressing "Email my list" to the email arriving.
  cook asks for the shopping list from web
  web asks for the shopping list from planner
    @engineer: POSTs /api/lists/send to
  planner reads the week's recipes from db
  db returns the recipes to planner
  planner hands the shopping list to mailer
  mailer sends the shopping list through mail
  mail emails the shopping list to cook
    > Usually within a minute.
    @exec > The cook has the list on their phone before they leave for the shop.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- walkthrough

walkthrough tour: A tour of Recipe box
  step big-picture
    > Cooks use one web app. Behind it are an API, a database and an email service.
  step big-picture: api
    > The **Recipe API** does the work: recipes, plans and shopping lists.
    @exec > The **Recipe service** is where the planning happens.
  step inside-api: planner, mailer
    > Inside it, the **Meal planner** builds the list and the **Mailer** sends it.
    @engineer >> Both are plain modules in one FastAPI process; nothing is queued.
  step send-list: 1-4
    > A shopping list starts with the week's recipes.
  step send-list: 5-7
    > Then it goes out by email.
